.TE
.SS "Kimi Code"
Audit mode is silent. Pass \-\-agent kimi, as the shipped entries do: a host
on kimi's older hook engine sends a payload shaped like Claude's. Only exit 2,
or exit 0 with a deny object, blocks; every other failure allows the action.
In enforce an unparseable event exits 2 and an input the guard cannot fully
classify is denied.
.PP
.TS
lB lB lB lB
lB l l l.
Event	Fires on	Enforce	Shipped
\&PreToolUse	\&tool call	\&deny	\&yes
\&UserPromptSubmit	\&submitted prompt	\&deny	\&yes
.TE
.SS "Cline"
Audit mode advises without deciding. The SDK runner behind the cline CLI sends
the snake_case names for the same files and never reads a prompt_submit
answer, so a prompt blocks only under the extension's own runner, which also
handles 4.x extension sessions. Since extension 4.1.26 a UserPromptSubmit
advisory reaches the model context. In enforce an event the guard cannot
classify is cancelled. The shipped files include POSIX shell and tested
Windows PowerShell hooks. Flip with skarn setup \-\-update \-\-agent cline
\-\-mode enforce.
.PP
.TS
lB lB lB lB
lB l l l.
Event	Fires on	Enforce	Shipped
\&PreToolUse	\&tool call	\&cancel task	\&yes
\&tool_call	\&tool call	\&cancel task	\&yes
\&UserPromptSubmit	\&submitted prompt	\&cancel task	\&yes
\&prompt_submit	\&submitted prompt	\&log only	\&yes
\&PostToolUse	\&tool result	\&cancel task	\&opt\-in
\&tool_result	\&tool result	\&cancel task	\&opt\-in
.TE
.SS "Copilot in Code"
Copilot in Code runs the Copilot CLI's hooks from each profile's hooks folder
and a folder project's .github/hooks. A preToolUse deny is honoured, a nonzero
exit fails closed, and a timeout let the held tool run. A would\-be ask is
answered with a deny on Code, where ask is unmeasured. These are Windows
measurements, on Copilot app `156.0.4314.58`. On Copilot app `158.0.4370.33`,
on Windows and macOS, a folder project's hook file fired in audit mode, and no
matching guard event was observed from a profile's hook file.
.PP
.TS
lB lB lB lB
lB l l l.
Event	Fires on	Enforce	Shipped
\&preToolUse	\&tool call	\&deny	\&yes
\&userPromptSubmitted	\&submitted prompt	\&log only	\&yes
\&postToolUse	\&tool result	\&advises only	\&opt\-in
.TE
.SS "Server-side agent runtimes (skarn envelope)"
You send one versioned envelope and read one JSON verdict object. Your client
applies deny or ask when enforce is true. Audit sets enforce false and blocks
nothing.
.PP
.TS
lB lB lB lB
lB l l l.
Event	Fires on	Enforce	Shipped
\&pre_tool_use	\&tool call	\&deny or ask	\&opt\-in
\&post_tool_use	\&tool result	\&deny or ask	\&opt\-in
\&user_prompt_submit	\&submitted prompt	\&deny or ask	\&opt\-in
.TE
.SS "Kiro CLI"
Pin \-\-agent kiro on every entry, because Kiro never auto\-detects. Exit 2
blocks a PreToolUse call, and every other event only advises. The V3 hook file
covers every V3 session, and a V2 session is covered only while it selects an
agent config that carries the hook. On Windows the adapter runs audit
semantics.
.PP
.TS
lB lB lB lB
lB l l l.
Event	Fires on	Enforce	Shipped
\&PreToolUse	\&tool call	\&deny	\&yes
\&UserPromptSubmit	\&submitted prompt	\&advises only	\&yes
\&PostToolUse	\&tool result	\&log only	\&opt\-in
\&Stop	\&response end	\&log only	\&opt\-in
\&SessionStart	\&session start	\&advises only	\&opt\-in
\&preToolUse	\&tool call	\&deny	\&yes
\&userPromptSubmit	\&submitted prompt	\&advises only	\&yes
\&postToolUse	\&tool result	\&log only	\&opt\-in
\&stop	\&response end	\&log only	\&opt\-in
\&agentSpawn	\&session start	\&advises only	\&opt\-in
.TE
.SH FILES
.TP
\fB~/Documents/Cline/Hooks/\fR
Cline's shared user hook directory, read by the extension and the CLI.
Documents is the literal folder joined to HOME; CLINE_DIR does not move it.
Setup writes only this user directory to avoid duplicate CLI invocations,
using executable PreToolUse and UserPromptSubmit files on POSIX or
PreToolUse.ps1 and UserPromptSubmit.ps1 on Windows. Doctor reports each file
as part of the four peer directories.
.TP
\fB~/.cline/hooks/\fR
Cline's CLI\-only user hook directory, relocated to <CLINE_DIR>/hooks when
CLINE_DIR is set. Doctor reads it as a peer of the shared user and two
workspace directories. Setup never writes here, because the CLI also reads
~/Documents/Cline/Hooks/ and would run duplicate hooks.
.TP
\fB.clinerules/hooks/\fR
Cline's shared workspace hook directory, read by the extension and the CLI.
Setup writes PreToolUse and UserPromptSubmit here with \-\-scope project, or
PreToolUse.ps1 and UserPromptSubmit.ps1 on Windows. Doctor reads it as a peer
of both user directories and .cline/hooks/.
.TP
\fB.cline/hooks/\fR
Cline's CLI\-only workspace hook directory. Doctor reads each file as a peer
of the other three hook directories; any cancel wins. Setup writes project
hooks only to .clinerules/hooks/.
